          "court": "Arizona Supreme Court",
          "year": 1984,
          "date_decided": "1984-05-29",
          "holding": "The Arizona Supreme Court approved the court of appeals' decision and held that records a public officer is required to keep are presumed open to inspection, subject to the custodian's discretion to deny access where confidentiality, privacy, or the best interest of the state outweighs disclosure, with any such refusal subject to judicial scrutiny.",
          "relevance": "Confirms that the records an agency is legally obliged to keep — the audit and expenditure trail — are precisely the records presumed disclosable.",
          "quote": "all records required to be kept under A.R.S. § 39-121.01(B), are presumed open to the public for inspection as public records",
